    "e-12421": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-12421",
      "knowledge_point_id": "74196b81-0e52-5d10-a099-ccd849d03a98",
      "knowledge_point": "Circulation Over Space Curves",
      "problem": "Calculate the circulation $\\Gamma$ of the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y,z) = y \\,\\mathbf{i} -x \\,\\mathbf{j} + z\\,\\mathbf{k}$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $\\mathbf r(t) =  \\sin (\\pi t)\\,\\mathbf{i} + \\cos (\\pi t)\\, \\mathbf{j} + t(2-t)\\,\\mathbf{k}$ for $t \\in [0,2].$",
      "worked_solution": "The circulation $\\Gamma$ measures the total work done by a force $\\mathbf F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\Gamma = \\oint\\limits_C \\mathbf F \\cdot \\textrm{d} \\mathbf r\n= \\int_a^b \\mathbf F(r(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf r'(t) \\; \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx = \\sin (\\pi t), \\qquad\ny = \\cos (\\pi t), \\qquad\nz = t(2-t) = 2t-t^2.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =y\\,i-x\\,j+z\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi t)\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi t)\\,j+(2t-{t}^{2})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf r'(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi t))\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi t))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =\\pi \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi t)\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi t)\\,j+2(1-t)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\u2032}(t) & =(\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi t)\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi t)\\,j+(2t-{t}^{2})\\,k\\,)\\cdot (\\pi \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi t)\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi t)\\,j+2(1-t)\\,k) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi t)\\cdot \\pi \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi t)+(-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi t))\\cdot (-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\pi t))+(2t-{t}^{2})\\cdot 2(1-t) \\\\  & =\\pi {cos}^{2}\u2061(\\pi t)+\\pi {sin}^{2}\u2061(\\pi t)+2(2t-{t}^{2})(1-t) \\\\  & =\\pi ({cos}^{2}\u2061(\\pi t)+{sin}^{2}\u2061(\\pi t))+2(2t-3{t}^{2}+{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\pi +4t-6{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0393={\u222e}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\pi +4t-6{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\pi t+2{t}^{2}-2{t}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[2\\pi +8-16+8]-[0] \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$",
